WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:08.130
56, 57, 58, 59...

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.820
Seira, are you busy?

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.240
What is it?

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.990
Well, I have a favor to ask.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.480
You do 200 sit-ups a day?!

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.440
I do that morning and night, 
so a total of 400.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.570
To make your ab muscles big and thick,

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.100
you have to apply resistance slowly.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.050
Oh, Luna-chan!

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.830
Where are you two going?

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:38.930
The training room.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:44.570
I asked Seira to teach me 
how to work out.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:48.940
It's better to be able to move 
properly when in battle, right?

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.070
Yeah.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.650
I'm going to do my best 
to make my body stronger!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.820
I see...

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.600
Do your best.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.330
See you later!

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.590
<i>So Seira-san actually 
opened up to Akari-san.</i>

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.440
<i>I wonder if Akari-san also...</i>

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.070
<b>A Lovely Holiday</b>

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:57.940
Is that true?

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.280
Indeed. There's no doubt about it.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.270
The Moscow branch contacted us. They said

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.580
the user of The Lovers
 tarot card disappeared.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.250
Does that mean the 
Daemonia ambushed her?

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.540
That's your job to find out, meow.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:18.840
We're only coordinators, meow.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.580
It's always like that.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.050
Writing reports without knowing 
who's going to read it,

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.700
and hearing something so 
important from someone

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.310
we've never even seen.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.930
This organization is

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:31.920
filled with significant 
risks for those girls.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.020
Those risks are, in turn, also 
protecting your fates.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.590
It's useless, Etia.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.820
Anyway, wouldn't it be better 
to think up a plan, meow?

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.530
The three sisters also 
said they had a report.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.670
Should we have Akari 
and the others present?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.640
We'll look into the matter 
first before talking to them.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.210
Until then...

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.320
Give them a little time.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.220
Talk about a surprise.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:12.640
Etia-san would never have given us 
a break like this before.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.460
Yeah.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.410
But, but, this is the 
first time the four of us

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.220
get to have a break together,

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.110
so let's have a lot of fun today!

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.820
Good point.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.480
Ow...

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.330
Akari-san!

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.830
Good grief. It's because you 
didn't hold on to the ring.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.290
Thanks, Seira.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.220
There we go.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.030
This is pretty fun.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:43.220
Let's have a lot of fun, 
okay, Ginka, Seira,

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.590
Luna-chan?

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.800
Right.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.720
I could have sworn it was 
around here somewhere.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.990
Oh, there it is.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.740
H-Hey, wait up!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.240
<b>Everyone Loves 
Stewed Pork Buns</b>

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:11.390
Wow, look at the line.

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.750
This place's stewed pork 
buns are to die for.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.480
Are we going to wait in line?

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.900
Of course! We're preparing 
for a long battle!

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.760
Thank you very much!

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.640
Lady, we'd like four of 
the stewed pork buns!

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.000
I'm sorry. I just sold the last ones.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.370
What?!

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:37.560
But...

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:38.900
But we got in line.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.300
I'm really sorry.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.230
Too bad.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:49.930
And we were almost there. 
Ugh, I'm so mad!

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.230
Th-That's...

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:55.340
...the fan that you can 
only get at Sancho Panza's

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:57.460
once in a year summer event!

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.000
Yeah, it is.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.960
And it even has President Shirokane 
Yataro's signature on it!

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:02.950
<b>Shirokane Yataro</b>

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:06.330
I'm a huge fan of Yataro-san.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.870
I can totally relate to 
the way he lives his life,

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.180
and he's cheered me up many times.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.520
Is there any way you 
could give that to me?

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.850
Huh? Uh, sure...

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.520
Really? Thank you!

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.860
But, in return...

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:24.860
It looks so delicious.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.410
Thanks for the food!

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:31.870
It's so good!

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.940
The pork is so soft.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.870
It's great that it was 
 just steamed, too.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.500
Man, we lucked out since he
 was such a great guy.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.880
Guess there aren't any bad 
people among fans of my Pops.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.260
Such a waste! What are you doing?!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.760
Make sure you enjoy it, 
my little ant friends.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.460
Here.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.520
Eh? Are you sure?

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:01.340
There's a lot of fat in stewed pork.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:03.270
Thank you!

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.090
I'll give you some of 
mine, too, Akari-san.

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:11.980
No, that's okay. I'm already full.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.280
Thanks though, Luna-chan.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.290
Then I'm totally calling dibs!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:24.190
These are the profiles of the two 
Daemonia that Meltina-oneetan

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.500
and Priscilla-oneetan 
exterminated recently.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:31.270
It's rare that two appear 
at once, so we investigated.

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:36.260
And both of them were friends 
of Ginka-oneetan's dad.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.680
Dad!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:40.750
Eh? Both of them? Coincidentally?

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:43.560
Up until now, I thought 
the places and reasons

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.770
they were infected 
were totally separate.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.170
Precisely.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:48.650
That's why it's strange.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.700
It means that intentions are 
functioning in the Daemonia.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.620
The Lovers card user disappeared.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:02.870
We're still looking into it, but 
apparently she was annihilated.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:04.230
But...

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:07.800
Annihilation isn't even 
recorded in the books.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.260
It's become obvious that the 
Daemonia have a will

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.510
and are purposely trying to attack us.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:17.150
That can't be... They're supposed 
to be like viruses, right?

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:18.630
They can't have intentions.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:23.670
It could just be the Daemonia's 
defensive instincts are at work,

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.260
but it's dangerous to go 
in with any preconceptions.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.870
A temple caught on fire because 
lightning struck it... Is it a curse?

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:35.320
Speaking of curses, you heard about 
the train losing control, right?

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.670
How scary.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:37.830
It's hot...

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.380
I can't do this anymore.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:42.580
Let's get something cold 
to eat and rest somewhere.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.310
We just ate the stewed pork buns.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:48.960
Who cares? Hey, perfect timing.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.960
<b>Nagataki Jingling Ice Cream</b>

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.170
Seira, let's go!

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.300
Are you okay?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.310
Yes.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:01.690
I'm glad you and Seira-san 
are friends now.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:02.400
Yeah.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.520
After we talked about the Daemonia,

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.830
I think we understand 
each other a little better.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.230
I see...

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:12.490
Wait, Onee-chan!

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:18.440
I have an older twin sister.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.990
She's cheerful and kind.

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:26.500
She might be a little 
like you, Akari-san

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:29.630
It makes me happy to hear that.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.250
Is your sister back at your house?

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.630
Yes, something like that.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.240
I see.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.510
Sorry to keep you waiting. Here!

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.890
Nagataki's famous jingling ice cream!

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.230
Thank you.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:49.090
Thanks, Seira. Oh, money, uh...

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.780
I'm sorry. I don't 
have any more money.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:56.610
Same here...

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.630
None...

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.190
For crying out loud, 
you guys are hopeless.

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:03.490
I thought something like 
this would happen, so...

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.540
Ta-da!

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:56.170
The country is truly coming upon 
the time of revolution.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:00.260
Let us not fear it. Let us 
accept it, and change!

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.260
So cute.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.400
We're matching.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.010
This is great, isn't it?

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:03.680
Yeah!

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.680
<b>The Time is Now for Revolution 
Member of the New Philanthropy Party</b>

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.680
<b>Hakamaten Ichiro</b>

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.540
I'm going to take good care of it.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.690
Let's see, where should we go next?

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.180
We went to quite a few 
places, didn't we?

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:14.440
I'm hungry...

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:17.840
Oh, no. I don't have any more.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.510
Then we should probably 
head back... Huh?

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:27.200
Another line?

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:29.490
I guess they're waiting 
for their fortunes.

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:33.830
Oh, could that be...

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.210
Mama Nagataki?

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.720
A-Akari!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.180
I was so surprised to see you!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:55.090
I had no idea you guys were 
telling fortunes there.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:56.790
Since it's been so busy,

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:59.560
Mama Nagataki's been 
putting it all on us

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.990
and was trying to take a break.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.280
It's always like that.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:09.200
Oh, but I went out to buy 
Castella for everyone.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.190
And if I hadn't gone out, 
I wouldn't have

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:13.750
run into Akari, right?

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.130
There you go again...

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.300
Yeah, you shouldn't skip out on work.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.180
But man, that was quite a line.

00:12:22.180 --> 00:12:24.260
You guys must be making a fortune.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.640
You're too blunt, Ginka.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:29.400
What a funny kid.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:33.350
Our house burned down in a fire,

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.940
so we've got to work and do our best.

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:39.190
We all started over again from nothing.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:43.270
Looking back, the fire might 
have been a turning point.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:47.200
We were able to rent a place in 
such a nice area because of it.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.830
I'm sorry.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:51.950
I never had the chance to 
see you all after the fire.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.290
No, it's fine.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.710
You were okay, and that's 
all that matters.

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:02.580
So you're all going to the same 
fortune-telling school as Akari, right?

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:03.980
That's very admirable.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:06.110
I just learned everything on my own.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.430
I'm happy for you.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.180
You were able to meet friends 
with similar dreams.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.180
Yes.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:17.280
Hey, why don't you tell 
them their fortune?

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:19.260
As their fortune-telling senior?

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.940
Good point. Since you're here, 
I'll read your fortune.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:24.710
Really?

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:26.540
Thank you very much!

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:30.170
Oh, but we don't have any money...

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.030
You can just pay later.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:37.950
Just come back when you've grown.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:40.710
Okay? Our future fortune-telling ladies.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.390
Thank you so much, Auntie!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.470
Nothing less from our 
senior! So manly!

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.220
Cash...

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:06.490
It looks like you've all 
been through quite a bit.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.490
I don't know exactly what, but...

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:12.770
The Strength card is in 
the position of the past,

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.500
with The Devil card under influence,

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:19.040
meaning you knew you 
had to accept someone,

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.000
but in the end, you couldn't.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.300
Something like that.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.370
Judgment means rebirth,

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:29.510
or your efforts are finally paying off.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.850
Currently, you all have better 
opinions of each other

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.280
and are in a good state.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:37.780
There's nothing better than if you can

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.770
take your relationship to the fullest.

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:41.330
However...

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:46.700
The World, The Tower,

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.530
and The Chariot cards 
are reversed, and The Moon...

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:55.020
You all understand the meaning 
of these cards, right?

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:57.540
Well, there are a lot 
of interpretations.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:00.820
But the future can change.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:04.080
As long as you believe in each 
other and stick together,

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.550
everything will be fine.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.050
Oh, it's already this late?

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:16.210
Why don't you have dinner with 
us, since you're already here?

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:17.590
You have the day off, right?

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:20.380
Yeah. Why not spend the night, too?

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:21.640
Spending the night, huh?

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:23.810
But I wonder if that'll be okay.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.680
I'll call Etia-san.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:31.950
And we're going to 
help in the negotiations!

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.610
I guess it's too difficult to say.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:41.580
I think Akari realized something, too.

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:43.660
Completion and destruction...

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.880
All that lies ahead of 
them is destruction.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.970
I have no idea what exactly 
lies in their future.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:54.660
If those girls will summon 
something from within themselves,

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:58.470
or if they'll have trouble 
from the outside...

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:02.350
And when you try to see, 
there's some kind of haze.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:06.860
Right. It's like there's some 
great power in the way.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:11.860
It could be

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:17.870
that the time they'll be able to 
spend like that will be short.

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.870
Yes, please don't worry.

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:25.600
We ate so much.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.800
I totally remembered how it used to be.

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:29.800
Thank you for the meal.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.550
The chicken salad was delicious.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:34.500
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:39.060
Hey, why don't we play a game 
to work off what we just ate?

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:48.200
Once you get through this 
forest, there's a statue.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:51.660
There's something hidden 
in the statue's pedestal.

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:53.450
You just have to bring that back.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.460
What do you think?

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:56.880
Th-That's...

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:59.910
A test of courage?

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.200
Yeah, something like that.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:04.320
Perfect for summer, isn't it?

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:10.950
Good point. I'd rather 
take a bath and go to bed.

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:14.720
The prize is Fukudaya's premium 
Castella. How about it?

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:15.500
I'm in!

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.460
Well, do your best!

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:20.020
We're off...

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:24.480
I-It's so dark with just the candle.

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:30.070
I-I can't... I can't do this.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:33.840
What do you mean, you can't? You 
fight Daemonia all the time.

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.490
Demons and ghosts are different!

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:39.370
Akari-san, it'll be 
okay. I'm here for you.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.460
Luna-chan, that's not me.

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:57.620
Oh, these are the Lil' Disembodied 
Souls we sell at our place.

00:17:58.040 --> 00:17:59.640
Four for 398.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.020
They found us out! Oh, goodness.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.530
But it's still creepy.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.570
L-Let's hurry!

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.610
This place is even scarier!

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:28.500
Something came out!

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.140
I-It multiplied! No!

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:39.800
S-Seira, I-I can't breathe!

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:41.760
It has to be those two.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:55.900
A ghost!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.670
Hey! That's rude!

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.150
Oh, sorry.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.510
We're here.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.770
Let's hurry back.

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:12.040
I wonder what's there?

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.810
There won't be any ghosts, right?

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.750
A picture?

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:28.070
Hey, this is...

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:28.970
Akari-san?

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:30.810
What is it?

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:34.610
So cute!

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:43.320
No!{dame!}

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.460
A-Akari-san!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.010
No fair going back by yourself!

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:48.410
Wait!

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:51.890
Jeez! That's so mean, Aunties!

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:56.160
Who are you calling mean? 
You called me a ghost!

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:59.350
Now, now. You guys won the game.

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:00.670
Here you go, Castella.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:07.180
Thanks for the food!

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:14.970
Well? Were you able 
to have a little fun?

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:16.430
Yes!

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:27.990
Such a great view.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.450
So wonderful.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:34.290
I'm glad we got to spend the 
whole day yesterday together,

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:37.850
and get to know each other better.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.480
Talk about a weird fate.

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:49.200
The four of us were just gathered 
to exterminate Daemonia.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:53.630
If we had lived normal lives, 
we probably wouldn't have met.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:57.980
We share the same powers, 
and the same secret.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:20:59.370
And that's why we

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:03.520
want to know each other 
better and become closer.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.630
No matter what happens in the future,

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:11.830
as long as the four of us 
are together, we can do it.

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:19.500
All of you come back sometime.

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:21.420
Thanks, Auntie.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.150
Thank you for taking care of us.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:38.310
Going against fate...

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.170
...might be hard, but...

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:45.980
Please let those kids find happiness.

00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:50.780
We're back!

00:21:51.050 --> 00:21:53.740
That was so much fun!

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:55.700
Good morning.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:59.890
Oh, good morning. Sorry we're late.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:03.100
Gather in the meeting room. There's 
something we need to discuss.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:07.730
It's an important matter that has 
to do with all of your futures.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:28.450
<b>The Magician card implies original 
ideas, inquisitiveness, and freshness.</b>

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:42.220
<b>#01 The Magician</b>

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:28.110
I'm Etia.

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:28.920
I'm Ariel.

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:33.200
<b>It is usually treated as the first 
tarot card, and signifies the beginning
of everything or new situations, 
as well as infinite possibilities.</b>

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:31.510
Hey, what were your 
hobbies again, Ariel?

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:35.650
Me? You've been with me so many 
years, you should know by now.

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:38.200
<b>If you were to choose this card, 
it shows that you'll have a positive 
attitude and will to be able to bring
 out your potential in a new environment, 
opening up a new path for yourself 
and the success that will follow.</b>

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:38.100
Um, I have no idea!

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:41.390
<b>The Overflowing Water</b>

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:38.720
Huh?

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:40.200
<b>However, if the card is reversed, 
please rethink the situation if you 
are about to start something 
or take action.</b>

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:40.320
See you next time!

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:42.520
<b>Is there a possibility that you are ill 
prepared or you're acting prematurely? 
Let's not do anything rash and start 
again after you've polished yourself.</b>
